    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0169" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1922: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-19T20:00:00-04:00">October 19, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. Your 327, October 17. Department concurs in your recommendation regarding
                    assurance to be given Iranian Government if Sheridan determines wheat supply
                    will be insufficient to last until <pb facs="0170" n="158" xml:id="pg158"/> next
                    harvest. However, you should give no guarantee to Iranians pending further
                    instructions. We are sending summary of your telegram to London and instructing
                    London Embassy to endeavor to obtain British agreement to joint assurance.
                        Winant<anchor n="51" xml:id="d175-f1"/> at Cairo is also being informed and
                    authorized in his discretion to take question up with British Middle East
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d175-f1" n="51" xml:id="d175-f1-content">
                <p>Frederick Winant, United States civilian representative on Middle East Supply
                    Center.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
